# Pinned QEMU dist OCI artifact.
#
# Consumed by scripts/fetch-qemu-dist.sh. Sourced as shell so values must
# be plain `key=value` (no inline comments on value lines).
#
# To bump (run all from the qemu source root):
#   1. ./contrib/apple-vfio/scripts/make-dist.sh
#      Produces a fresh ./dist/ + ./dist.tar.gz.
#   2. ./contrib/apple-vfio/scripts/publish-qemu-dist-to-ghcr.sh
#      No args needed — the script defaults the tag to
#      `git describe --always --dirty --abbrev=12` of the qemu tree, so
#      the registry tag carries the source provenance. The script then
#      prints the exact QEMU_DIST_TAG + QEMU_DIST_SHA256 values to paste
#      below.
#   3. Paste the printed values, commit.
#
# Tag carries source provenance (you can `git checkout <tag>` and
# rebuild). Sha locks the actual binary content — two clean builds of
# the same commit can still differ (toolchain, embedded timestamps),
# so we keep both.
#
# QEMU_DIST_SHA256 is the sha256 of the layer blob (= sha256 of the
# .tar.gz). The fetch script verifies BOTH that the tag's manifest
# references this digest AND that the downloaded blob hashes to it, so
# a registry that repoints the tag (deliberately or otherwise) can't
# slip a different artifact past us.

QEMU_DIST_REPO=ghcr.io/scottjg/qemu-vfio-apple-dist
QEMU_DIST_TAG=v11.0.0-rc1-749-g7e013ad0cdcd
QEMU_DIST_SHA256=7cfa9e50f2e1bcb26408ecb9f69ccbd909d4093085112045721c921b42b0ed28

